# boat

> Product home for boat: persistent Linux VM sandboxes for AI agents.

boat gives AI agents persistent Linux (Ubuntu) VMs: SSH and SCP access, Docker inside the VM, a public IPv6 address and outbound IPv4, a 60fps virtual desktop, and fast disk-level fork from a snapshot. Sandbox compute is billed per second at $0.036/h for 4 vCPU / 8 GB, with no compute charge while stopped. boat offers a 7-day free trial with a card (25 compute hours), then plans from $20/mo.

Limits: machines in Germany, Finland and France only (no US or Asia region); no GPU; starts per day capped by plan (create, fork and resume each count); auto-stop defaults to 1 hour; a stopped disk is kept for at least 14 days; the disk is saved every minute and at stop, so a machine failure loses the writes after the last snapshot. Details: https://docs.boat.dev/limits

## Docs

- [Docs index](https://docs.boat.dev/llms.txt): every docs page, each fetchable as markdown
- [API reference](https://docs.boat.dev/api/v1): human-readable API guide
- [SDKs](https://docs.boat.dev/sdks/overview): Python and TypeScript clients

