- [boat vs Unikraft Cloud: full agent VMs vs millisecond microVMs](https://boat.dev/compare/boat-vs-unikraft-cloud): boat vs Unikraft Cloud: full VMs with Docker, /dev/kvm, SSH and coding agents, against microVMs that Unikraft says boot in milliseconds and sleep when idle.
- [boat vs Mastra: a full VM for agents, not a framework](https://boat.dev/compare/boat-vs-mastra): Mastra is a TypeScript agent framework with hosting and on-demand sandboxes. boat gives each agent a full VM with Docker, a desktop and preinstalled coding agents.
- [boat vs Datalayer: Linux VMs vs Jupyter runtimes for data agents](https://boat.dev/compare/boat-vs-datalayer): boat vs Datalayer: a full Linux VM with root, Docker and coding agents installed, against Jupyter-based runtimes and agent applications for data analysis.
- [boat vs Expo: long-running agent VMs vs mobile build jobs](https://boat.dev/compare/boat-vs-expo): Expo's EAS runs mobile app builds on fresh VMs, and builds stop at 2 hours on paid plans. boat gives agents a Linux VM that keeps its disk and runs Docker.
- [boat vs Archal: a real VM vs simulated SaaS APIs](https://boat.dev/compare/boat-vs-archal): boat gives an agent a full Linux VM with Docker, root and coding agents built in. Archal gives it fake, stateful copies of GitHub, Slack and Stripe to test on.
- [Build an Issue-to-PR Software Factory on boat](https://boat.dev/blog/software-factory): OpenFactory turns GitHub, Linear, and Sentry issues into planned, tested, independently reviewed pull requests. Learn how to deploy and customize the pipeline on boat.
- [Containers vs VMs: why your agent sandbox should be a real machine](https://boat.dev/blog/containers-vs-vms): AI agents run untrusted code, need Docker, and keep long-lived state. A look at where container sandboxes break down, how microVM sandboxes compare, and why boat gives every agent a full VM.
- [Benchmarking Five Sandbox Providers with a Devin-Style Agent Build](https://boat.dev/blog/integration-benchmark): A boat-funded study, run in June 2026: a coding agent built a Devin clone on boat, E2B, Daytona, exe, and Islo. Build costs, times, error rates, and which sandbox lifecycles worked.

## Machine-readable files

- [Agent contract](https://boat.dev/auth.md): auth rules agents must follow
- [OpenAPI spec](https://boat.dev/openapi.yaml): public boat API surface (YAML)
- [Public plans](https://boat.dev/api/plans): plan prices, quotas, and concurrency ceilings (JSON, no auth)
- [Sitemap](https://boat.dev/sitemap.xml): every indexable page on this site

## Install the boat CLI

- macOS / Linux: `curl -fsSL https://boat.dev/install | sh`
- Windows: `irm https://boat.dev/install.ps1 | iex`
